# Runtime secrets. The skill pulls these from the prod container at the start of a
# run and wipes them at the end (SKILL.md steps 0 and 3). If a run is interrupted
# between those two steps, a live OPENAI_API_KEY and a live Basecamp token are left
# sitting in the working tree, one `git add -A` away from being committed. The wipe
# is the primary control; this is the one that still holds when the wipe never runs.
.oaikey
.bctok

# Per-project run artifacts. The skill writes these next to its own scripts, so
# without this they show up as untracked noise in every `git status` and invite
# being swept into an unrelated commit. They are outputs of a run, not part of the
# skill, and they carry client project detail that has no reason to be in the repo.
scripts/*-deep-plan.json
scripts/*-published.json
scripts/gen.log
scripts/gen_output*.log

# Per-project story configs. EXAMPLE.json is the template and IS tracked; every
# other config here describes a specific client build.
story_configs/*.json
!story_configs/EXAMPLE.json
